<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia budget proposes 50 rgt credit card charge.</title>
<headline>Malaysia budget proposes 50 rgt credit card charge.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian Deputy Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim proposed a 50-ringgit a year service charge on all credit cards in the 1997 budget unveiled in parliament on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Smart cards and credit cards are extensively used,&quot; Anwar said. &quot;But it shoulD not lead to indebtedness. The number of credit cards exceeds two million.</p>
<p>&quot;As a measure to encourage prudence, I propose that a service tax of 50 ringgit a year be imposed on all types of credit cards, including those given on a complimentary basis,&quot; Anwar said. -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom 603-201-4813</p>
</text>
